lly with the cold I've got at the moment). From your description I'm imagining my voice like Draco's from Dragonheart.<br /> <br /> As for other people's voices, I can't help but imagine <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> 's as being reminiscent of my long-time English teacher and mentor. He's got this patient, calm sort of voice that is perfect for explaining things and which seems to lengthen words when I'm being stupid, as if to help me understand. Heaven knows I need it sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T11:58:58-07:00","id":930962,"title":"","content":"Surprised no ones done me yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T18:12:15-07:00","id":931112,"title":"","content":"Should I start a new thread for voice clips? Because I feel like recording myself again, and I'm taking requests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T19:21:17-07:00","id":931138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=930914#post930914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for other people's voices, I can't help but imagine <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> 's as being reminiscent of my long-time English teacher and mentor. He's got this patient, calm sort of voice that is perfect for explaining things and which seems to lengthen words when I'm being stupid, as if to help me understand. Heaven knows I need it sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow.... That's actually pretty spot-on for me at my best moments. Of course, I have an easier time getting my ideas across through writing than speaking, so there's that ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T01:39:29-07:00","id":931242,"title":"","content":"Oh, funny thing. I was playing a game with a friend and he said my voice was spot on identical to his old history prof, to the point he almost felt he was back in the class.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T06:05:20-07:00","id":931302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=930962#post930962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprised no ones done me yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that you don't have an avatar is probably part of it. Even if your username is well-known, people don't tend to remember you as well if they don't have an image to associate with the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:05:54-07:00","id":931360,"title":"","content":"I shall have to get that corrected...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:22:53-07:00","id":931368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>garhkal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=931360#post931360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shall have to get that corrected...</div> </div> </div> </div>Much better. Anyway, my immediate version of your voice - almost certainly because of the picture - is quite a firm, strong one with the sort of 'twang' that you always get from ex-military people. That's probably a mile off the mark, but that's my image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T14:20:22-07:00","id":931577,"title":"","content":"Maybe. I don't have any twang i know of.. Heck my english side of my accent is so assimilated into my american accent you can barely hear it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T18:26:59-07:00","id":932720,"title":"","content":"Oddly enough, despite growing up in the very heart of Appalachia, I don't have an accent nor did I as a kid. Maybe it's because I was raised by television. That and my parents were careful to lose their accents in their teen years, well before I was born.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T01:11:14-08:00","id":1060783,"title":"","content":"Hm. I don't think that I &quot;read&quot; with voices. Knowing that certain people do so is incredibly perplexing for me. But I have major problems with both visual and audio &quot;mind imagining&quot; [I can't recall or create images and sounds in my mind], which might be source of the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T09:05:52-08:00","id":1060900,"title":"","content":"Here's hoping my voice has changed, for obvious reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T10:42:56-08:00","id":1060932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=932720#post932720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly enough, despite growing up in the very heart of Appalachia, I don't have an accent nor did I as a kid. Maybe it's because I was raised by television. That and my parents were careful to lose their accents in their teen years, well before I was born.</div> </div> </div> </div>I likewise grew up in Appalachia but my accent story is a little more complicated. Neither of my parents were from Appalachia originally and both being from educated backgrounds had a well-meaning but kind of condescending disdain for it, so they fastidiously corrected me any time I would adopt a twang or an aphorism. I was also a bookish kid and tended to have an elevated affect anyway. As I went through school though I found this made me a target, so eventually after years of bullying I'd had enough and consciously assimilated into the local vernacular to the point that it was second nature, helped along by spending a lot of time out in the woods with the scouts. It was still noticeably my speech, no one was ever going to mistake me for a good old boy, but I had enough accent that I didn't stick out of a crowd. Then late in adolescence I started spending more time outside of Appalachia and people would make fun of me whenever a twang or an ain't would slip out. I was stuck, and it made me self-conscious. So I started walking back the way I came, deliberately suppressing the accent I'd gone out of my way to adopt. Now what I hear all the time is &quot;Oh you're from West Virginia? You don't sound like it at all!&quot; To which I can only reply &quot;Yeah, I get that a lot.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T16:36:38-07:00","id":1066029,"title":"","content":"I'm still struggling with the idea that people read with &quot;voices&quot; and that &quot;voices&quot; aren't intellectual assumptions and metaphors about essence of the particular text bit born from parsing it and putting it in the context of the profile we have for that person, but it made me curious; is there anyone who &quot;reads&quot; me with a voice? How does it, um, sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T18:24:28-07:00","id":1066083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=1066029#post1066029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still struggling with the idea that people read with &quot;voices&quot; and that &quot;voices&quot; aren't intellectual assumptions and metaphors about essence of the particular text bit born from parsing it and putting it in the context of the profile we have for that person, but it made me curious; is there anyone who &quot;reads&quot; me with a voice? How does it, um, sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I often see you posting analyses of crunch, and you seem like a calm and focused person. Your user images further add to the feel of a collected scholar. But you also show a sharp sense of humor sometimes. The overall mental sound is close to that of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q76evm7Qtws\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Velma from Scooby-Doo Mystery Inc</b></a>, but nowhere near as nasal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-21-2017, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T19:33:51-07:00","id":1066096,"title":"","content":"I get a girl from an anime tone. Like the one with glasses who's logical.<br /> <br /> It's obviously heavily biased by the avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T21:35:37-07:00","id":1066121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=1066029#post1066029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still struggling with the idea that people read with &quot;voices&quot; and that &quot;voices&quot; aren't intellectual assumptions and metaphors about essence of the particular text bit born from parsing it and putting it in the context of the profile we have for that person, but it made me curious; is there anyone who &quot;reads&quot; me with a voice? How does it, um, sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm pretty sure the &quot;voices&quot; we read text with are absolutely intellectual assumptions and metaphors about essence of the particular text bit born from parsing it and putting it in the context of the profile we have for that person. But &quot;voices&quot; is just easier to write out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, your posts have a very even and collected tone to me. Not unlike Spock in cadence, but higher in pitch. The pitch is in a pretty middle range, neither deep and masculine nor high and feminine. Not monotone though. I think I agree with nofather in the assessment of &quot;like the token intellectual anime girl&quot;, with the caveat that it'd definitely be the version from the English dub, because that character's voice in the sub would almost definitely be too high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-22-2017, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:32:10-07:00","id":1066325,"title":"","content":"Hey, I asked some people around me and they stared at me with that question mark in their eyes, wondering if I'm pulling their leg; &quot;of course I vocalize in my head, it's like, I can't even imagine not doing it&quot;. Don't laugh :C.<br /> <br /> I see that my avatars certainly contributed to the image. I actually love that Velma thing, I need to watch this incarnation of Scooby. I always respected her in original cartoons. Gonna show these descriptions to my friends and ask them what they think about it, they will probably stare at me again blinking slowly :P. Thank you all for sharing this with me, it's very interesting experience. <br /> Also it's kinda reassuring, because the traits you all mentioned are things I kinda like and would aspire to be, if that makes sense. <br /> ...though I need to check out some Spock videos, because when it comes to Star Trek, I'm the Picard person, so Spock is less of a icon to me than Data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:37:25-07:00","id":1066383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=1066325#post1066325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I asked some people around me and they stared at me with that question mark in their eyes, wondering if I'm pulling their leg; &amp;quot;of course I vocalize in my head, it's like, I can't even imagine not doing it&amp;quot;. Don't laugh :C.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I did not mean to make fun of your reaction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=1066325#post1066325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when it comes to Star Trek, I'm the Picard person, so Spock is less of a icon to me than Data.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, but Data's speech pattern is too awkward and stilted for your posts, with his inability to use contractions and general air of bemusement about everything. Spock has a similar cool logic, but is far more collected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:45:08-07:00","id":1066389,"title":"","content":"I have to hand it to you WHW, I was too afraid to look conceited if I asked what people thought my voice sounded like, and then you just go and do it and everybody was cool with it. XD You make it look easy.<br /> <br /> So yeah...I'm curious what people think my &quot;voice&quot; is like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:51:37-07:00","id":1066397,"title":"","content":"Torbj\u00f6rn from Overwatch without the accent. Basically fantasy dwarf voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T14:51:20-07:00","id":1066584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=1066383#post1066383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I did not mean to make fun of your reaction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Same here, but Data's speech pattern is too awkward and stilted for your posts, with his inability to use contractions and general air of bemusement about everything. Spock has a similar cool logic, but is far more collected.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Takes a beat for Critical Failure on a Joke roll*.<br /> It was supposed to be funny. *<br /> <br /> *failure to make a joke is a joke in itself, ah ha! :P<br /> <br /> BDH, don't worry, I had similar doubts but then I scanned threads history to check how received were similar questions in the past to boost my confidence! <br /> ...Gibbering Eloquence, it might be because I'm not wearing my glasses, but for whatever reason, my brain tries to assume that Xenomorphs mouth is on the other side of it's head in your avatar. Probably because it's the point where human eye is drawn when looking at a image (I think it was slightly up-to-right from the center?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T15:20:02-07:00","id":1066594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/879121-do-you-have-specific-voices-in-your-mind-for-other-users?p=1066584#post1066584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Gibbering Eloquence, it might be because I'm not wearing my glasses, but for whatever reason, my brain tries to assume that Xenomorphs mouth is on the other side of it's head in your avatar. Probably because it's the point where human eye is drawn when looking at a image (I think it was slightly up-to-right from the center?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, me too! I actually didn't realize it was a xenomorph for a long time, instead seeing a weird anteater-like creature. Even after realizing it was a xenomorph I still have a tendency to think of it as the weird creature my brain invented to make sense of the picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T18:33:46-07:00","id":1066658,"title":"","content":"The Xenomorph's mouth in my user image is facing the left.<br /> <br /> \u200bI haven't formed a precise mental voice for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1923_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1923\" data-vbnamecard=\"1923\">BigDamnHero</a> yet, but judging from their name and current user image, my impression is that of a confident and dignified person that others would look up to, like a 2ED Fairest Changeling.<br /> <br /> How do you all currently imagine my &quot;voice&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}